  "id": "sr",
  "term": "S–R",
  "definition": "S–R means stimulus–response. In psychology of learning and habits, it refers to a link in which a particular cue comes to trigger a particular action, especially after repeated reward-based training; behavior governed mainly by this link tends to be relatively insensitive to changes in the value of the outcome or in the response–outcome contingency.",
